15 CSS Tricks That Save Me Hours Every Week
Not animations or fancy effects. Practical solutions to real layout problems.
1. Truncate Text With Ellipsis
/* Single line */
.truncate {
white-space: nowrap;
overflow: hidden;
text-overflow: ellipsis;
}
/* Multi-line (works in modern browsers) */
.truncate-2 {
display: -webkit-box;
-webkit-line-clamp: 2;
-webkit-box-orient: vertical;
overflow: hidden;
}
2. Center Anything (The Modern Way)
/* Flexbox — works for everything */
.center {
display: flex;
justify-content: center; /* horizontal */
align-items: center; /* vertical */
min-height: 100vh;
}
/* Grid — even simpler */
.center {
display: grid;
place-items: center;
min-height: 100vh;
}
3. Sticky Header/Footer
/* Stays visible when scrolling */
.sticky-header {
position: sticky;
top: 0;
z-index: 100;
background: white; /* Important: opaque background */
}
.sticky-footer {
position: sticky;
bottom: 0;
}
4. Scrollbar Styling
/* Webkit browsers (Chrome, Safari, Edge) */
.custom-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar {
width: 8px;
}
.custom-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar-track {
background: #f1f1f1;
border-radius: 4px;
}
.custom-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {
background: #c1c1c1;
border-radius: 4px;
}
.custom-scrollbar::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {
background: #a1a1a1;
}
5. Aspect Ratio Without JavaScript
/* Before: padding-bottom hack (ugly) */
.aspect-old {
position: relative;
padding-bottom: 56.25%; /* 16:9 */
}
/* Now: aspect-ratio property */
.video-container {
width: 100%;
aspect-ratio: 16 / 9;
background: black;
}
.square {
aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
}
6. Smooth Scrolling
/* Entire page */
html {
scroll-behavior: smooth;
}
/* Or specific container */
.scroll-container {
scroll-behavior: smooth;
overflow-y: auto;
max-height: 400px;
}
7. Selection Styling
::selection {
background: #3b82f6; /* Blue */
color: white;
}
/* Brand-colored selection looks professional */
8. Focus Visible (Accessibility)
/* Show focus ring only when using keyboard, not mouse click */
:focus-visible {
outline: 2px solid #3b82f6;
outline-offset: 2px;
}
/* Remove default outline for mouse users */
:focus:not(:focus-visible) {
outline: none;
}
9. Container Queries (Game Changer)
/* Component that adapts to its PARENT, not the viewport */
.card-container {
container-type: inline-size;
}
@container (min-width: 400px) {
.card {
display: grid;
grid-template-columns: 200px 1fr;
gap: 1rem;
}
}
@container (max-width: 399px) {
.card {
/* Stack vertically on small containers */
}
}
Why this matters: A card can be full-width on a sidebar but grid-layout in a main column. Same component, different parent widths.
10. Logical Properties (Internationalization)
/* Instead of direction-specific properties */
.box {
margin-inline-start: 1rem; /* margin-left in LTR, margin-right in RTL */
padding-block-end: 0.5rem; /* padding-bottom regardless of direction */
inset-inline-start: 0; /* left in LTR, right in RTL */
text-align: start; /* left in LTR, right in RTL */
}
11. Dark Mode (One Line)
@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
:root {
--bg: #1a1a2e;
--text: #eaeaea;
--accent: #3b82f6;
}
}
/* Or use the newer light-dark() function */
:root {
color-scheme: light dark;
--bg: light-dark(#ffffff, #1a1a2e);
--text: light-dark(#1a1a2e, #eaeaea);
}
12. Reduced Motion (Accessibility)
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
*,
*::before,
*::after {
animation-duration: 0.01ms !important;
animation-iteration-count: 1 !important;
transition-duration: 0.01ms !important;
scroll-behavior: auto !important;
}
}
Always include this. Respect user preferences.
13. Print Styles
@media print {
/* Hide non-essential elements */
nav, footer, .no-print, .sidebar {
display: none !important;
}
/* Reset colors for printing */
body {
background: white;
color: black;
}
/* Show link URLs */
a[href]::after {
content: " (" attr(href) ")";
}
/* Avoid page breaks inside content */
h1, h2, h3, img, figure {
break-inside: avoid;
}
/* Remove backgrounds to save ink */
* {
background: transparent !important;
box-shadow: none !important;
}
}
14. Custom Checkboxes & Radio Buttons
/* Hide native appearance */
input[type="checkbox"],
input[type="radio"] {
appearance: none;
width: 20px;
height: 20px;
border: 2px solid #ccc;
cursor: pointer;
position: relative;
}
input[type="checkbox"]:checked,
input[type="radio"]:checked {
background: #3b82f6;
border-color: #3b82f6;
}
/* Custom checkmark */
input[type="checkbox"]:checked::after {
content: '✓';
position: absolute;
color: white;
font-size: 14px;
top: 50%;
left: 50%;
transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
}
/* Radio button dot */
input[type="radio"] { border-radius: 50%; }
input[type="radio"]:checked::after {
content: '';
position: absolute;
width: 10px;
height: 10px;
background: white;
border-radius: 50%;
top: 50%;
left: 50%;
transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
}
15. The "Just Works" Reset
*, *::before, *::after {
box-sizing: border-box;
margin: 0;
padding: 0;
}
html {
scroll-behavior: smooth;
}
body {
min-height: 100svh; /* Better than 100vh for mobile */
line-height: 1.6;
-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
}
img, picture, video, canvas, svg {
display: block;
max-width: 100%;
}
input, button, textarea, select {
font: inherit;
}
p, h1, h2, h3, h4, h5, h6 {
overflow-wrap: break-word;
}
a {
text-decoration: none;
color: inherit;
}
ul, ol {
list-style: none;
}
/* Useful utility classes */
.visually-hidden {
clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
clip-path: inset(50%);
height: 1px;
overflow: hidden;
position: absolute;
white-space: nowrap;
width: 1px;
}
Quick Reference Card
| Problem | Solution | Lines |
|---|---|---|
| Center anything |
display: flex/grid + place-items
|
3 |
| Truncate text | text-overflow: ellipsis |
3 |
| Sticky element | position: sticky |
2 |
| Responsive components | Container queries | 5 |
| Dark mode |
light-dark() or media query |
3 |
| Smooth scroll | scroll-behavior: smooth |
1 |
| Print-friendly |
@media print rules |
12 |
| Accessible focus | :focus-visible |
3 |
| Reduced motion | prefers-reduced-motion |
8 |
| Aspect ratio | aspect-ratio: 16/9 |
1 |
Which CSS trick saves YOU the most time? Drop it in the comments.
Follow @armorbreak for more frontend tips.

